  "notes": "Source data includes Employee Annuitants, Surviving Spouse Annuitants, and Reversionary Annuitants. The target 'Retirement' definition typically excludes beneficiaries (spouses/reversionaries). However, the document does not provide a separate 'Service Retirees Only' table with annual benefit totals; it only provides these three separate tables. To provide the requested distribution of members receiving benefits, all three tables are transcribed. The mapping sums all counts and all benefit dollars across these three populations to produce the grid. Note: The 'Under 55' row in the Employee Annuitants table is mapped to the '50-54' target row, assuming the majority of this group falls within the 50-54 range as per standard actuarial binning conventions for retirement data, though the exact split is unknown. Reversionary annuitants under 30 are excluded from the target grid as they fall below the 50-54 minimum.",
